{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"broadcast","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncBroadcastSequence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncBroadcastSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent22AsyncBroadcastSequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncBroadcastSequence"},{"type":"text","text":" that multicasts elements to multiple consumers concurrently."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This operator enables multicasting of values from the upstream sequence to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiple consumers that iterate concurrently. Each consumer sees the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence of elements, and elements are only fetched once from the upstream"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"broadcast"},{"type":"text","text":" creates a new shared sequence that manages buffering and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distribution of elements to all active iterators. A consumer receives the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements the shared sequence reads from the upstream after the consumer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"creates its iterator; elements already read and handed out are not replayed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"broadcast","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"share","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" operators are functionally equivalent and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be used interchangeably.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading"},{"code":["\/\/ Create an AsyncStream that emits 3 random values between 1 and 5","let upstream = AsyncStream<Int> { continuation in","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.finish()","}","","let sharedSequence = upstream.broadcast()","","async let firstConsumer = Task {","    for await value in sharedSequence {","        print(\"First consumer received \\(value)\")","    }","    \/\/ prints the values the shared sequence reads after this consumer subscribed","}","","async let secondConsumer = Task {","    for await value in sharedSequence {","        print(\"Second consumer received \\(value)\")","    }","    \/\/ prints the values the shared sequence reads after this consumer subscribed","}","","\/\/ A consumer that subscribes after the shared sequence has handed out values misses them.","await firstConsumer.value","await secondConsumer.value"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Deferred\/broadcast()"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:Sci7Afluents8SendableRzsAB7ElementRpzrlE9broadcastAA22AsyncBroadcastSequenceVyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO8DeferredV","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/ShareSequence.swift#L68","fileName":"ShareSequence.swift"},"conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"broadcast"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent22AsyncBroadcastSequenceV","text":"AsyncBroadcastSequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"extendedModule":"_Concurrency","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["_Concurrency"],"name":"Afluent"}],"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","title":"broadcast()"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a sequence that multicasts elements to multiple concurrent consumers."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Deferred"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/deferred\/broadcast()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncBroadcastSequence":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncBroadcastSequence","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AsyncBroadcastSequence","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncbroadcastsequence","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncBroadcastSequence","title":"AsyncBroadcastSequence","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async sequence that multicasts elements from an upstream sequence to multiple concurrent consumers."}]},"doc://